ideas.team_fit:
Utshab owns the kernel, candidate retrieval and certification. This is essentially ANN and IR engineering.

Laraib and Rhea own:
- downloading and concatenating the 13 Allen h5ad files and joining the cell metadata on cell_label (scripted, with a template);
- the course-required documentation of source, variables, preprocessing and label tier for every dataset;
- defining rare subclasses and the label-hierarchy mapping;
- running Scanpy and Seurat-sketch baselines from provided notebooks;
- biological inspection of clusters where MI and PCA-Leiden disagree, checking markers against the Allen taxonomy;
- figures and report sections.

13-week plan:
- Weeks 1-3: kernel, plus exactness on PBMC14K and Zeisel.
- Weeks 4-7: candidate generation, recall study, D2 runs.
- Weeks 8-10: baselines and rare-type analysis.
- Weeks 11-13: writing.

